{"author":"Rebar Bot Nava","author_email":"joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com","author_id":"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d","data":{"body":"Landed as Gerrit change 3106, commit 1f452719aa7 (LLM-Review +1 with no advisories, Verified +1, 0 unresolved). Reproduced first with real keys before any change: a certificate signed under a pinned key marked revoked verified as certified with trust_basis pinned_environment in advisory mode AND under verify.require_environment, so revocation was ignored even when the gate restricts trust to pinned keys. Cause: d909 added the revoked-key filter for the own principal only. Fix: _opcert_trust_root now passes unrevoked_only=True for every principal. 2 of the 3 new tests fail on the old code (advisory mode reported pinned_environment; enforcement certified); the forged-payload control and an unrevoked pinned key behave as before. 41 tests in the three opcert files and 739 opcert/attestation tests pass. make verify locally: only the 17 known pandoc failures, no errors; Linux CI green. Limits: no key-era check, so a certificate signed BEFORE the key's revocation is also refused under enforcement (fails closed, same rule the operator chose for the own principal in d909); in advisory mode, the project default, such a certificate still verifies on its embedded key like any unpinned one (c21f design). Enforcement is not enabled in this project today, so live impact was low."},"env_id":"492a5c71-6cda-48a6-8134-02ff6a672739","event_type":"COMMENT","timestamp":1792921217368119001,"uuid":"5a6c8038-0bd9-457e-89de-12cc82c093c3"}